  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Science for Sustainable Development in SEE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UNESCO underscores the critical role of science in tackling today&#x2019;s urgent economic, social, and environmental challenges, recognizing that no single country can achieve sustainable development alone. In regions like Southeastern Europe and the Mediterranean, countries face unique challenges, such as climate change impacts, water scarcity, and biodiversity loss, compounded by economic disparities and migratory pressures.  To address these needs, UNESCO will promote science, technology, and innovation (STI) as key drivers for sustainable development, particularly through its International Science Programmes (ISPs). With projects tailored to national and regional priorities, countries will be technically supported to develop and apply innovative solutions and STI policies that enable more climate actions, biodiversity conservation, freshwater resource managements, and disaster risk reduction.</narrative>
  </description>
